From: Musicalista <musicalista@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0006/0006] security/amfi: bypass AppleMobileFileIntegrity and cs_enforcement for test userland

Disable CS_ENFORCE, CS_RESTRICT, and CS_KILL enforcement flags in the Darwin
kernel policy module. Allows executing custom unsigned ARMv7 Mach-O binaries,
debugging with task_for_pid(0), and loading non-Apple signed extensions on
the ported Samsung Galaxy Tab 4 10.1 (SM-T530) platform.
---
 src/main.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -210,6 +210,36 @@ void amfi_bypass_init(void) {
+    pe_kprintf("[AMFI] cs_enforcement_disable = 1\n");
+    pe_kprintf("[AMFI] cs_debug = 1\n");
+    pe_kprintf("[AMFI] amfi_get_out_of_my_way = 1\n");
+    pe_kprintf("[SECURITY] Code signature enforcement bypassed for non-Apple hardware.\n");
+}
